Short:        Stress benchmark for minigl.library
Uploader:     marcus.gerards@googlemail.com (Marcus Gerards)
Author:       marcus.gerards@googlemail.com (Marcus Gerards)
Type:         util/moni
Version:      0.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1
Distribution: Aminet
Requires:     minigl.library 29.1 (RadeonGL 0.12 or later recommended);
              a 68020 or better with an FPU
Kurz:         Stresstest-Benchmark fuer minigl.library

GLBench 0.1  --  8 November 2026


WHAT IT IS

A stress benchmark for minigl.library 29.1. Seven scenes, each leaning on
another part of the 3D card, and one score: five keep their shapes on the
card and leave it the work, two measure the bus. Together the scenes use
every feature RadeonGL, the minigl.library for the ATI Radeon 8500 to
9250, offers. Burn runs one scene for ten minutes and checks all the while
that the picture stays right.


THE SCENES

  1 Pelt      a furred ring in a breeze: 20 alpha-tested, blended shells
              from two textures -- the fill rate
  2 Lanterns  eight lights over a waving banner kept on the card, two
              passes, fog -- the card's transform and lighting
  3 Chrome    sphere-mapped bodies kept on the card, plinths from nested
              display lists, labels by polygon offset -- texgen
  4 Embers    soft sparks in four quarters, each blending another way
              (add, subtract, min, max) -- blending, points, wide lines
  5 Plasma    a plasma sent every frame, a turning palette, every texture
              format and environment -- texture uploads
  6 Swarm     1920 darts kept on the card, the last third for red/cyan
              glasses -- geometry
  7 Mirror    every frame read back from the card and drawn again -- the
              bus, both ways

Frames are counted, not timed: every machine draws the same frames.


THE SCORE

Each scene's frames a second against a reference machine's (an A4000
with a 68060 and a Radeon 9200 behind a Mediator, 640 x 480 x 16); the
geometric mean of the seven ratios times 1000. In 0.1 the reference
figures are provisional. The result goes to RAM:GLBench-Result.txt as
well, with the machine, the library and the screen mode.


BURN

Pelt for ten minutes. Every 250 frames one fixed frame is drawn, read back
and compared with the first: a card running too hot or a bus losing data
shows up as a picture error. The Radeon has no temperature sensor;
GLBench reads none.


INSTALLING

None: unpack the archive anywhere and double-click GLBench or GLBench-Burn.
They choose the 68040/68060 or the 68020/68030 build themselves. From a
Shell, C/GLBench takes options (scenes, frames, screen size, a window,
pictures of every scene): see GLBench.guide.


SOURCE CODE

In the drawer Source (no icon), and with RadeonGL:
  https://github.com/bubbob42/RadeonGL
It builds with m68k-amigaos-gcc and the MiniGL 29.1 SDK.


HISTORY

0.1  First version: seven scenes, the score, Burn with picture checks.
